PCI-VME Adapter Bridges AlphaServer to VMEbus

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides a Digital AlphaServer 2100 with access to a wide variety of
   VMEbus cards

o  Provides a cost effective way to share memory and special purpose boards
   between a PCI local bus computer and a VMEbus system

o  Takes full advantage of PCI system resources for VMEbus applications

o  Supports software for either DEC OSF/1 or OpenVMS platforms

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Alpha AXP users often require connectivity to the wide variety of cost
effective specialized I/O devices available on the VMEbus. In addition,
users need to directly access these devices with the highest possible
performance from Alpha AXP based servers, using their preferred operating
system.

Digital offers a PCI to VMEbus adapter that consists of two cards; one card
plugs into a PCI slot of an AlphaServer 2100 system and the other card
occupies a 6U slot in a VME cardcage. The two cards are connected via a
cable. Digital includes the appropriate support software, Digital PCI-VME
Adapter driver, for either the DEC OSF/1 (SPD 61.54) or OpenVMS (SPD 61.53)
operating system.

This two-card set and associated software create an I/O bus that functions
the same as a local I/O bus. The programmer treats this VMEbus the same as a
native bus.

BENEFITS

o  The performance of an Alpha AXP server coupled with the richness of the
   VMEbus environment.

o  It is as easy to prepare a device driver for a VME device running on a
   Digital host as it is to prepare such a driver for any other competitive
   system.

o  Users who need to connect a VME peripheral to a workstation or other
   system can now do so with minimal effort. Over 4,000 options are
   available from some 300 vendors.

o  A very high degree of compatibility with other Digital VME interface
   products, TURBOchannel-based or single board computer, protects existing
   investments in device driver software and applications.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The PCI-VME Adapter is available now and includes the adapter driver
software license for either OpenVMS or DEC OSF/1 systems. The complete
package includes an eight foot cable, software media, and documentation.
Users who have purchased the adapter hardware directly from Bit 3 Computer
can order the software separately from Digital.

Most users will likely need a cabinet kit of cables and connectors
appropriate to the particular VME chassis, which will be used with the
PCI-VME Adapter to meet regulatory requirements on electro-magnetic
interference. Digital does not currently offer such kits, which can be
directly purchased from Bit 3 Computer.

The PCI-VME Adapter can also be ordered as an integrated system, with a
rackmount Digital 2100 Server, VME cardcage, storage, etc. Contact your
local Custom Systems and Solutions specialist.

