SERVICES

The PCI-VME Adapter is supported worldwide by Digital's service organization
and covered by Digital's standard warranty terms and conditions.

In addition, Digital's engineers can work with users to identify and
evaluate various alternative solutions to a given VMEbus challenge. They are
called upon frequently to develop some or all of the software required to
complete a system solution. They can also design specialized hardware
modules, and can provide unique power and packaging solutions.

TECHNICAL DATA

o  Hardware is Bit 3 Computer Corporation Model 617.
o  Bidirectional random access bus mastering from either system.
o  Hardware byte "endian" swapping.
o  Hardware mapping registers:
   8K for PCI to VME, programmed I/O;
   4K for VME to PCI, Slave mode Direct Memory Access (DMA);
   4K for VME to PCI, Controller mode DMA.
o  Supports 8, 16, and 32 bit data transfers.
o  Each bus can operate independently.
o  Memory-mapped I/O is supported, with restrictions.
o  Direct Memory Access controller support, on-board or on VME controller;
   does not support concurrent activity for the on-board controller.
o  Multile PCI-VME adapters supported on a single system.
o  PCI adapter card, short form factor.
o  VMEbus adapter card, 6U form factor, meets IEEE 1014-C specifications.
o  Cable, 8-feet round EMI-shielded or 25-feet round EMI-shielded; custom
   lengths available from Bit 3.

