Digital AlphaServer 2100 4/190 VME

HIGHLIGHTS

o  High performance, scalable SMP system with a variety of high availability
   solutions

o  Both PCI and VME64 industry standard I/O for high performance flexibility

o  Similar functionality, price/performance and expandability as the Digital
   2100 systems

o  Conforms to ANSI/EIA and IEC standards for 19-inch rackmount

o  Can be ordered in either horizontal slide-out drawer configuration for
   space efficiency or vertical configuration for ease of access and service

o  Upgradable with future processor, memory, and I/O options as new
   technology is introduced in the Digital 2100 server family of products

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital AlphaServer 2100 4/190 VME system is a member of the Digital
2100 family. For realtime and embedded applications, it offers the popular
VME64 I/O bus in place of the EISA bus that is part of other Digital 2100
servers. It offers the flexibility of choosing over 4,000 existing VMEbus
options, combined with the high performance of the new PCI interconnect in
one integrated rackmountable system package. It has CPU, memory, and
standard I/O features and functionality, which are identical to the standard
Digital 2100 family. It offers 19-inch rackmount packaging for versatility
and reduced footprint. The AlphaServer 2100 4/190 VME system is supported by
DEC OSF/1 and OpenVMS operating systems.

The AlphaServer 2100 VME system is designed to handle virtually any
high-end, high performance application processing requirements. It is
particularly well suited to complex and demanding environments, such as
communications, aerospace and defense, and medical imaging.

For the communications environment, the large memory -- for memory resident,
realtime databases -- and the vertical package that fits easily into the
Network Equipment Building Standard (NEBS) environment are ideal. Digital's
UNIX:OSF/1 offers SVID and SPEC 1170 compliance which is important to the
telecommunications user. In addition, the IEEE 1003.1b realtime extensions
and SMP support in OSF/1 provide a UNIX operating system with capability
unsurpassed by any competitor.

In the aerospace industry -- processing, air traffic control, and simulation
applications -- all require the capabilities that the AlphaServer 2100 VME
system offers. The user gets a compact single package for DSPs, realtime, or
special communication devices on the VMEbus, high performance graphics
options on the PCI bus, and the SMP computation capability that these
applications demand. Both OSF/1 and OpenVMS systems are widely used by this
industry.

Medical imaging is computationally intensive. Digital Signal Processing
(DSP) boards are often used to condition the signals before the images are
analyzed. All of the most powerful DSP boards are offered in VME form
factors, so they plug directly into the AlphaServer 2100 VME system.

Product Positioning

The AlphaServer 2100 VME system is the high end member of Digital's family
of VME products. The AXPvme-64 and AXPvme-160 single board computers provide
the traditional VME board level products. Combining the PCI to VME bridge
product with any AXP workstation provides a middle level of capacity. The
Digital 2100 VME multiprocessing server is the high end of the family for
the most demanding computational tasks.

The AlphaServer 2100 VME system complements the standard pedestal and
rackmount Digital 2100 systems that are configured with the EISA I/O bus
internally. The AlphaServer 2100 VME system is the first Alpha AXP server to
be designed specifically for the embedded and realtime market, offering
VMEbus connectivity and symmetric multiprocessing in an integrated package.
It shares all of the CPU, memory and standard I/O components of the Digital
2100 family of servers, and will be upgradable with future generations of
technology as they are introduced in the Digital 2100 family.

With its SMP capability, the AlphaServer 2100 VME system is a server for the
user of VME technology. If a user wants PCI and EISA, the AlphaServer 2100
family provides a solution to these needs. If an uniprocessor AXP
workstation with VME I/O is needed.

BENEFITS

The AlphaServer 2100 VME system offers the user the high performance and the
price/performance of an Alpha AXP symmetric multiprocessing computer
directly interfaced to the VMEbus, for use in today's complex, compute
intensive realtime and embedded applications. Applications that were not
possible with general purpose computers are now possible with the Digital
2100 VME server.

Symmetric multiprocessing offers computational capability that is
significantly more efficient and easier to program than the traditional
method of designing VME systems with multiple, loosely coupled, single board
computers. Because the AlphaServer 2100 VME system uses a private, very high
speed, internal bus for CPU to memory I/O, the VMEbus and the PCI are only
utilized for I/O operations, and the result is a balanced system design.

The AlphaServer 2100 VME system provides the bridge between the versatility
of VME and the high performance of the new PCI. Now the user can eliminate
the trade-off between performance and versatility. Both PCI options and VME
options can be used together in the same system package.

High capacity is the hallmark of the Digital 2100 VME server. Users can
configure the AlphaServer 2100 VME system with up to 4 CPUs, up to 2 Gbyte
of memory, and 4 Gbyte of internal disk storage, providing high capacity and
flexibility in the standard system cabinet. External disk storage and
additional expansion VME I/O cages can be rackmounted above or below the
system box.

The ability to configure the AlphaServer 2100 VME system with up to 2 Gbytes
of physical memory means that applications that manipulate very large data
items such as graphical images, radar signals, or realtime databases can now
perform the calculations directly in memory without time consuming disk I/O.

Over 4,000 VMEbus options from hundreds of vendors are immediately usable
with the AlphaServer 2100 VME system by plugging directly into the integral
VME64 I/O card cage included in the system box. For expansion beyond the 5
slots that are standard with the system, a PCI to VME bridge option is
available to connect the system to external VME card cages from any vendor
in the VME industry.

The Digital 2100 VME server is not Network Equipment-Building System (NEBS)
compliant. However, the vertical configuration may satisfy most user
requirements, with the exception of input power. Custom versions of the
Digital 2100 VME server suitable for these users can be offered at an
attractive price, depending on the firm requirements.

Operating system support for the AlphaServer 2100 VME system includes both
DEC OSF/1 and OpenVMS systems. Both operating systems offer realtime
features for building embedded and realtime applications. The VMEbus
interface is supported on both operating systems. The applications
programming interface for the internal VME64 and the external PCI to VME
bridge are the same, so porting of I/O devices among systems involves no
software changes.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Digital AlphaServer 2100 4/190 VME system is available now. It will be
available in volume shipments in February 1995. Users planning to use the
Digital 2100 VME server in their solution can develop their applications on
any Digital 2100 server with a PCI-VME Adapter.

Dress front covers (bezels) must be ordered separately, if they are desired
for finished appearance. Keyboard and mouse also are not included in the
packaged systems.

As a member of the Digital 2100 family of servers, the Digital 2100 VME
server supports all options supported on other Digital 2100 servers
according to the respective operating system Software Product Description,
except those that are EISA options.

