RAID and Write-back Cache for StorageWorks Array Controllers

HIGHLIGHTS

o  RAID and Write-back Cache options now supported on all HSJ series, HSD30,
   and HSZ40 array controllers

o  Controller based RAID dynamically shifts between RAID 3 and RAID 5
   algorithms depending on the I/O workload

o  Improves I/O response time by employing nonvolatile caching for write
   operations

o  Dual-path error handling improved

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Write-back Cache Option

The Write-back Cache option enables the existing read cache in a controller
to also cache data waiting to be written out to disk. It dynamically
allocates cache memory to both read and write operations simultaneously.
Write-back cache enables applications to continue working rather than
waiting for I/O completions, substantially boosting I/O performance for most
applications.

The Write-back Cache option includes a license, license key, and battery.
The software key activates the write-back capability provided in every copy
of the new version of the HS Operating Firmware V2.0, which is supplied via
a customer installable PCMCIA card. The battery protects data in the cache
that has not yet been written to media against loss due to power failure or
system failure for at least 100 hours.

RAID Options

RAID levels 3 and 5 typically are viewed as separate solutions suited to
different workloads. Digital's innovative implementation combines the best
of both. The RAID capability provided by HS Operating Firmware V2.0
dynamically adjusts between algorithms to maximize performance for
applications that require high throughput or high bandwidth. The RAID
firmware option employs parity protection to maintain availability of data
from multiple disks, even if one of the disks fail.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Later this month letters or faxes announcing the new capabilities supported
by V2.0 of the HS Operating Firmware will be sent to all users who have
HS-series controllers. The letters will include a form to be completed and
returned for shipment of the new firmware release. This will be the fastest
way for all users -- including those who have maintenance contracts -- to
get the new release. No automatic distribution will be made.

Users who wish to receive HS Operating Firmware V2.0 must return the PCMCIA
card containing a previous HS Operating Firmware release after verifying
proper operation of the new one. A pre-paid, pre-addressed mailer is
provided with every firmware upgrade.

Ordering the Write-back Cache Option

Some early HSJ40 controllers will need new cache modules to be able to
implement write-back cache. Digital will upgrade early-version cache at no
extra charge. Users should use the controller command, "SHOW
THIS_CONTROLLER" to see which cache version they have. Version 1 cache
modules must be upgraded; version 2 modules are ready for the Write-back
Cache option. THe Write-back Cache options include license, key, and
battery. Users who need the upgrade should use the first two order numbers
below, which furnish a new module along with the license, key, and battery.

To obtain cache for controllers bought without cache, order HSxxx-XD to
receive a 16 Mbyte read cache, or HSxxx-XF to obtain a 32 Mbyte read cache,
then order the appropriate Write-back Cache option to receive the battery,
license, and software key to activate write-back cache.

To add more cache to controllers with 16 Mbyte cache, order HSxxx-XE to
obtain a 32 Mbyte cache module (requires return of 16 Mbyte cache), then
order the appropriate Write-back Cache option to obtain battery and license.

When ordering the RAID firmware option, please note that a Write-back Cache
option must be present in a controller in order for RAID firmware to
function.

