Software License Simplification

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Changes to Digital's licensing, pricing, and upgrading of its software
   products -- effective October 10, 1994

o  Simplifies the software offerings on VAX and Alpha AXP systems

DESCRIPTION

Software License Simplification consists of four changes to current software
business practices:

o  Simplified License Structure
o  Simplified License Pricing
o  Simplified License Types
o  Simplified License Upgrade and Migration

Simplified License Structure

Digital is simplifying its license structure by replacing 22 VAX and 6 Alpha
AXP tiers with three system classes: Workgroup (includes entry-level
servers) Departmental, and Enterprise. These system classes reflect logical
processor groupings based on user computing environments. Users can use the
same license across a much broader range of systems -- both within the
system class, and any lower system class. There is no charge for license
upgrades within a system class when upgrading hardware. Users will see a
significant reduction in the number of times a license transaction is
required.

The following list identifies the system class for existing systems:

