Evolving the Frameworks For Leadership Open Client/Server Solutions

To solve the most common client/server problems that users face, Digital
provides world-class networked software for multivendor, heterogeneous
environments. Digital has the software products that provide added value and
differentiated competitive advantage.  This software announcement provides
you with computing choices that work together better and easier than anyone
else.

Working with users, business partners, and standards bodies, Digital created
open software frameworks that integrate the necessary components for
effective, multivendor client/server solutions. Today, Digital takes the next
step by announcing products and technologies within these software frameworks
that:

o  Differentiate Digital in the marketplace.
o  Highlight Digital's core competencies in distributed systems, multivendor
   integration, networked software, and scalability.
o  Protect existing software investments.

Over the past year, Digital has populated these frameworks with open
client/server software products. Let's briefly review the software
integration frameworks and the major capabilities and products that they
provide:

o  Workgroup Integration -- groupware or client/server software that
   automates information access, collaboration, and the sharing of tasks
   across workgroups through integration. Workgroups typically include users
   who need to share resources in a team environment. Workgroup products
   include ALL-IN-1, TeamLinks, LinkWorks, DEC Notes, and DEC VTX products,
   plus a number of tightly integrated third party applications.

o  Messaging Integration -- standards-based messaging software for connecting
   desktops, business applications, and trading partners. Products include
   MAILbus 400 and DEC X.500 for reliable, manageable store and forward
   messaging backbones; MAILworks for providing a rich set of services to the
   user's choice of mail clients and mail-enabled applications; and DEC/EDI
   for providing application-to-application exchange of structured business
   documents between trading partners.

o  Network Integration -- software that provides the supporting foundation
   for implementing distributed client/server computing across the
   enterprise. Products include the PATHWORKS product portfolio, DECnet/OSI
   and X.25 products, TCP/IP on OpenVMS, InfoBroker, and IBM interconnect
   products.

o  Management Integration -- software for managing multivendor PC LANS to
   enterprise systems and distributed networks. Based on international
   standards, these solutions consolidate and integrate management tools
   across multivendor systems and networks, simplifying the management of
   applications, databases, networks, systems, storage devices, and other
   resources. POLYCENTER solutions portfolio of products are Management
   Integration products.

o  Data Integration -- tools that simplify development and deployment of open
   client/server data access and integration solutions across database
   systems of different vendors. Products include the ACCESSWORKS family of
   products -- DEC DB Integrator, DEC DB Integrator Gateways, DEC Data
   Distributor, and DBA Workcenter.

o  Production Integration -- the tools for integrating all the essential
   components of a mission-critical, open client/server solution such as
   transaction processing. The Production Integration framework provides
   solutions for data management, transaction monitors, continuous computing,
   as well as presentation, development, and analysis tools. Products include
   the Reliable Transaction Router, ACMS, and DECADMIRE.

o  Technical Integration -- tools that support tasks such as high performance
   parallel computing and client/server software development and runtime
   environments.

Today's software announcement underscores Digital's leadership in open
client/server solutions -- Digital makes user computing choices work together
better than anyone else.


