TeamLinks Mail for Windows Integration with Lotus Notes

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Systems integration service

o  Brings TeamLinks and Digital Mail Services to Lotus Notes users

o  Allows existing TeamLinks for Windows users to add Lotus Notes to the
   desktop

o  Works with either DEC MAILworks or ALL-IN-1 servers

SERVICE DESCRIPTION

Many users have a large investment in their existing ALL-IN-1 and MAILworks
systems and MAILbus backbones. This new service allows the products to
integrate with Lotus Notes by providing TeamLinks Mail for Windows as a
replacement for the mail system used by Lotus Notes. It preserves the
investment in ALL-IN-1, MAILworks, and MAILbus products, while extending
these services to the Lotus Notes desktop.

After a user selects a document to be mailed from within Lotus Notes, the
TeamLinks Mail for Windows "create/send window" is displayed. After the
message is sent, the user is returned to the Lotus Notes application. Lotus
Notes mail enabled applications are also supported.

If a Lotus Notes/TeamLinks user receives a Notes document in their TeamLinks
Mail inbox (in Lotus Notes native format) from another user, TeamLinks will
call the Lotus Notes application to display the document with all of its
formatting and field information intact.

This service also provides format translation for recipients who are not
Lotus Notes users. ALL-IN-1, MAILworks, and TeamLinks for Windows users can
receive documents as Microsoft Rich Text Format (RTF) files, which can then
be viewed with such formatting as fonts, bolding, and underlining intact.
This translation is a manual process done at the time the user sends the
note following the standard Lotus Notes mechanism.

BENEFITS

o  Users with investments in ALL-IN-1, MAILworks, or MAILbus systems can
   preserve these investments while taking advantage of the capabilities of
   Lotus Notes.

o  Existing Lotus Notes users can move to a more robust enterprisewide mail
   system without impacting the usage of Lotus Notes.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

This capability is delivered as a service by the local Digital consulting
group and will be available in late September.

