TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.2

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Streamlining ALL-IN-1 processes by automating workflow now extended to
   client/server implementations

o  V1.2 allows TeamLinks Routing clients for Windows and Macintosh to use
   ALL-IN-1 as their mail and routing server

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The ALL-IN-1 server provides all the mail, directory, and file services to
distributed TeamLinks clients as well as to traditional VT clients.  Users
can now add routing and tracking capabilities within a mixed desktop
environment by adding TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.2 (SPD #33.75.02).  The
TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 server now supports three clients -- TeamLinks
Routing for Windows and Macintosh, along with the current ALL-IN-1 VT user
client.

Digital's solution for mail-enabled workflow is TeamRoute.  TeamRoute is
capable of routing any document stored in an ALL-IN-1 Integrated Office
Server file cabinet to any user on the network.  The document can be a form,
word processing document, image, CAD drawing, or spreadsheet.  The
originator of the routed item specifies the routing list and the document is
then routed in the order specified.

During the review process, each reviewer is granted specific processing
rights or requirements based on roles.  By assigning roles, the originator
can selectively specify privileges for actions to be taken by any reviewer
on the document.  For example, the right to add or remove additional
reviewers may be granted.

As a document is processed, its actual location and status may be determined
by anyone on the routing list who has been assigned this privilege or role.
This capability enables users to dramatically decrease the time spent
tracking documents during the review cycle.

New Features

o  The ability to use TeamLinks Routing for Windows V2.1 and Macintosh V2.0
   and V2.1 clients with the TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 server.

o  ALL-IN-1 Integrated Office Server V3.0 and V3.1 support on the OpenVMS
   VAX platform only (plans for TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 support on the
   OpenVMS AXP platform are under development).

o  Maintenance fixes in both the TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 server and client.

BENEFITS

TeamRoute is a convenient "out-of-the-box" application. V1.2 allows
Macintosh and Windows clients to:

o  Electronically route live data forms or finished documents for electronic
   signature approval -- Speeds the time necessary to complete business
   processes, decreases cost of handling paper, and protects documents from
   access, manipulation, or fraud.

o  Use existing ALL-IN-1 mail services -- Standardized transport; protects
   existing investments in enterprise networks; reviewers are not restricted
   by LAN implementation.

o  Track progress and status of a routed item -- Higher level of control
   over the business process.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

TeamRoute for ALL-IN-1 V1.2 server supports VT clients and is available now
in two license types: Traditional (based on capacity) or Personal Use.  PC
clients must be purchased separately.

