MAILbus 400 Message Router (XMR) Gateway on OpenVMS VAX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Gateway for ALL-IN-1 systems requiring access to MAILbus 400 backbone

o  Provides the basis for a smooth evolution from a backbone based on
   Digital's Message Router to MAILbus 400, conforming to the 1992 X.400
   standards

o  Uses DEC X.500 Directory Services for address translation

o  Maximizes the throughput of messages via the MAILbus 400 Message Transfer
   Agent (MTA)

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital has a very large installed base of users whose electronic messaging
systems are based on the MAILbus 1 and ALL-IN-1 product sets, both of which
use the Message Router message transport to connect to other private and
public electronic messaging systems.  Many of these users wish to upgrade to
Digital's MAILbus 400 and DEC X.500 Directory (SPD #40.77) products, which
implement the latest technology, conforming to 1992 and 1993 CCITT/ITU
standards. These products operate on both OpenVMS VAX and DEC OSF/1 AXP
platforms, thus providing price/performance leadership.

The MAILbus 400 Message Router (XMR) Gateway (SPD #53.65) provides a direct
high performance link between the MAILbus 1 message transport (Message
Router) and MAILbus 400 Message Transfer Agent (SPD #42.83), enabling users
in the MAILbus 1 environment to begin using the services available in the
new product set. The MAILbus 400 XMR Gateway seamlessly connects the MAILbus
400 based messaging system to the environments served by Message Router,
enabling applications that use Message Router such as ALL-IN-1 software to
exchange mail with native X.400 based applications.

The MAILbus 400 Message Router (XMR) Gateway performs address translations
using information held in the X.500 directory used by the MAILbus 400 MTA.
It translates between all forms of Digital's Message Router and O/R
(originator/recipient) addresses, allowing users in either electronic mail
network to address users in the other network using their own natural
addressing style.

The XMR Gateway provides a customizable bodypart mapping table to transfer
all bodyparts without conversion. Typical Digital document formats such as
WPS-PLUS and DDIF and tagged PC formats such as WordPerfect and Microsoft
Word are transferred from Message Router to MAILbus 400 as tagged
"Externally Defined" bodyparts so that receiving applications can recognize
them. In the reverse direction, X.400 bodyparts are placed into Message
Router format and tagged so they can be understood by viewers and
converters. Users are able to add new bodypart types to this table as
required.

The XMR Gateway differs from the Message Router X.400 Gateway (MRX) in
several areas:

o  XMR Gateway is simpler to manage (it is not required to do conversions)
   and has a higher message throughput.
o  XMR maps all Message Router bodyparts to their equivalent X.400
   bodyparts.
o  Addresses are translated using data in the DEC X.500 directory rather
   than Digital's Distributed Directory Service (DDS).
o  It is part of the MAILbus 400 product set which means consistent
   management, installation, and configuration procedures.

As users evolve to a MAILbus 400 based backbone, they will be able to phase
out use of the MRX Gateway. Over time, the dominant component of the system
will be the MAILbus 400 backbone. This will be realized through the
availability of a wider range of products that directly connect to MAILbus
400 via the XAPI interface, thus displacing many existing MAILbus 1 gateways
with better price/performance offerings.

BENEFITS

Because the XMR Gateway provides a seamless connection between the Message
Router and MAILbus 400 environments, Digital users begin benefiting
immediately from the latest standards and technologies, higher performance,
enhanced management and administration, and lower cost of ownership. Users
may begin to plan the implementation of an open client/server full X.400 or
X.500 messaging and directory system without disrupting their business.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The MAILbus 400 Message Router (XMR) Gateway is available now on the OpenVMS
VAX.

