LinkWorks Developer Options

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Announcing the LinkWorks Evaluation Kit

o  Introducing LinkWorks Software Components

PROGRAM DESCRIPTION

The LinkWorks Partner Program is a dynamic software program that offers
unprecedented access to Digital and database vendor software and services
for systems integrators, network integrators, developers, and consultants.
The program provides:

o  Demo to try LinkWorks and database software.

o  Technical support.

o  LinkWorks training.

o  Access to the most current technical and product tools.

Introducing LinkWorks Software Components

LinkWorks Software Components is a leading-edge technology that allows
developers to easily develop reusable software components. LinkWorks
Software Components make it easy for integrators and developers to create
custom groupware solutions in a fraction of the time it normally takes, by
integrating their applications with the LinkWorks Solution Framework or by
customizing or extending the functionality of LinkWorks itself. LinkWorks
Software Components will be implemented in the upcoming release of LinkWorks
through the Application Programmable Objects.

The main goal for the LinkWorks Application Programmable Objects is to
provide programming openness. This opens the LinkWorks method engine to the
outside development community and makes it possible to integrate third party
code into LinkWorks. Developers can take full advantage of LinkWorks' object
oriented framework while using their favorite development tools such as
Microsoft Visual Basic or C++.

The LinkWorks Application Programmable Objects provide the ability to extend
and reuse the LinkWorks Solution Framework by:

o  Providing a programmable interface to the LinkWorks functionality. This
   programmable interface can be accessed through such standards as
   OLE 2 Automation, DDE, and DLL. This allows seamless integration between
   application programs and LinkWorks.

o  Making it possible to extend the out of the box LinkWorks functionality
   by changing internal LinkWorks methods. This is a powerful way to derive
   customized functions from the standard LinkWorks functionality.

o  Providing user scripting and system batch capabilities to enable
   automation of repetitive or complex tasks.

Access to Application Programmable Objects will initially be through the
LinkWorks Software Developer Kit. This will allow integrators and developers
to build something once for a multivendor computing environment, use it many
times in different situations, and easily modify it to meet new needs. The
kit will lower development costs and accelerate time-to-market for workgroup
applications. The LinkWorks Applet Sampler, part of the Software Developers
Kit, gives developers concrete examples written in Visual Basic and C++ of
how to use Application Programmable Objects.

LinkWorks V3-beta Evaluation Kit

The LinkWorks V3-beta Evaluation Kit makes it easy to understand
LinkWorks and the business opportunity it provides. Developers can start
developing software components to the LinkWorks environment. The Evaluation
Kit contains both CD-ROM and hard copy.

The CD-ROM contains:

o  LinkWorks V2.1 for DEC OSF/1 V2 server and MS-Windows clients.
o  LinkWorks V3-beta for DEC OSF/1 server and MS-Windows clients.
o  ORACLE 7 runtime database.
o  Updated demos for selected industries, based on V3-beta.
o  Simple automated installation procedures (installs in less than 30
   minutes).
o  LinkWorks documentation (both V2.1 and V3 draft).
o  Updated V3-beta Demo and Integration Guide and Service Guide.
o  Software Developer Kit, including interface manuals, programming
   examples, and workbench.

The hard copy includes:

o  Draft of LinkWorks V3 documentation.
o  ORACLE documentation.
o  Updated V3-beta Service Guide and Demo and Integration Guide.
o  Software Developer Kit interface manuals.

