PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows Clients

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Extends PATHWORKS product set with distributed computing infrastructure
   capabilities

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

PATHWORKS software allows PC users and administrators to integrate multiple
network operating systems, hardware, software, and network technologies,
providing enterprisewide information and resource sharing in a multivendor
environment. PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows client software (SPD
55.07.15), used on PCs running Microsoft Windows, Windows for Workgroups,
and DOS, provides information integration through file and printer sharing
and other networking operating system services, support for an access to
client/server and object-based applications, navigation tools for global
networks, and workgroup directory services. PATHWORKS software provides
network and system integration by offering the broadest set of clients,
servers, and networks out-of-the-box to integrate individual PCs and
workgroups with the enterprise. PATHWORKS software also includes powerful,
consistent management of multiple, different network operating systems from
a single, remote Windows workstation.

PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows client software includes many new
enterprisewide information integration features for end users,
administrators, and developers:

o  Through the inclusion of Mosaic, PATHWORKS software is now delivered
   "Internet ready" so that end users can easily access information on the
   Internet's World Wide Web. (See the June 6, 1994, issue of Customer
   Update.) Mosaic is a global "browser" that allows end users to search for
   and retrieve, display, store, and forward documents and data from
   anywhere in the world via the Internet. Internet's World Wide Web is a
   diverse collection of information servers. End users will be able to open
   multiple windows for browsing independently from other windows. Through a
   series of pull-down windows, end users will be able to move quickly from
   one Internet location to another and customize windows to create and add
   to hotlists, print documents, and view document sources.

o  Through access to directory services for workgroups through the inclusion
   of InfoBroker for Windows, users now can look up employee information
   (and, with customization, resource information) in a simple and accurate
   manner. Workgroup directory services now can be implemented without
   lengthy and expensive implementation of global directory services yet
   also can be linked into global X.500 when the enterprise is ready.

o  PATHWORKS clients now are delivered 'enterprise ready' for information
   integration when developers develop client/server applications for
   multivendor environments. By including the following application
   integration client runtimes in the PATHWORKS client software, PC users
   are ready to take advantage of the client/server and object-oriented
   applications and global X.500 directory services, whenever the enterprise
   chooses to implement those.

o  ObjectBroker client runtimes for Windows use object-oriented technology
   to reduce application development and maintenance costs significantly in
   distributed environments and to deliver transparent application
   interoperability across multivendor common desktops and popular servers.

o  Distributed Computing Environment (DCE) client runtimes for Windows
   enables PC applications to use the multivendor resources of the
   enterprise whether they are UNIX, OpenVMS, other PC, or networked
   resources through Remote Procedure Calls (RPC) for distributed
   client/server applications.

o  DECmessageQ client runtimes for Windows offer reliable distributed
   client/server computing based on advanced message queuing technology.
   DECmessageQ enables Windows applications to integrate with distributed
   applications on multivendor platforms and provides guaranteed message
   communication.

The PATHWORKS V5.1 Software Developer's Kit for Windows is now available.
This kit provides application developers with a set of tools and APIs that
enables the creation of business solutions for integrating existing and new
applications and services in a distributed, heterogeneous environment. Refer
to the April 1994 issue of Customer Update for more information.

BENEFITS

o  Easy, cost effective connectivity of remote branch offices to the
   enterprise's wide area networks that gives the PC user full network
   operating system services and access to enterprise information through
   Digital's PATHWORKS X.25 and WAN ACCESS features.

o  Connectivity to PATHWORKS networks for mobile and wireless PC users
   through Digital's RoamAbout Mobile IP features. Portable computer users
   now can connect to their network and enjoy the same level of network
   services they have in their home office.

o  Selected PATHWORKS components in languages other than English now are
   available (CD-ROM distribution kit only).

o  Many PATHWORKS documents now are included in the PATHWORKS Family
   Information Shelf for easy, fast reference (CD-ROM distribution kit
   only). (Hard copy documentation kits are available separately.)

CHANNELS

PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows software is available through local
Digital sales offices and Digital's business partners.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows clients will be available in September
1994. The PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows CD-ROM distribution kit will be
available approximately two weeks prior to the diskette version.

Note that the limited time offer allowing upgrades from pre-V5 PATHWORKS for
DOS licenses (which grant access to PATHWORKS/LAN Manager servers) to
PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows (NetWare) Combination Client Server licenses
(which grant access to PATHWORKS/NetWare servers) has been discontinued.
Upgrades now are permitted only within the same NOS (LAN Manager or
NetWare).

To use the features of PATHWORKS V5.1 for DOS and Windows software, a client
license must be obtained for each PC. The V5.1 client license gives the user
the right to use the V5.1 client software and previous versions of PATHWORKS
client software (such as V5.0).

When users upgrade from PATHWORKS V4.x or earlier versions, license terms
and conditions change from "traditional license" terms and conditions to "PC
style" terms and conditions. The Combination Client Server license and
Client Network Services license also include the rights to use the PATHWORKS
Remote V5.1 for DOS and Windows product. Media and documentation kits are
available separately. Only one copy of the media and documentation kit is
required per network. Future versions of PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows
client software will only be available on CD-ROM.

