PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital is announcing a major release of its industry-leading ALL-IN-1
Integrated Office Server (IOS) -- V3.1. This new release runs on the OpenVMS
AXP platform which means users can take advantage of Alpha AXP processor
speed for improved performance, more users are supported by smaller boxes,
and lower maintenance costs.

The new ALL-IN-1 V3.1 mail server coupled with the TeamLinks for Windows and
Macintosh clients easily evolves ALL-IN-1 VT users to Windows and Macintosh
users, giving them all the benefits of client/server computing while keeping
the same ALL-IN-1 server. New end user features and options add more
leadership capabilities for users who remain on VT desktop devices. Plus,
ALL-IN-1 V3.1 includes improvements in system management.

New Features

o  Support for Alpha AXP platform with OpenVMS software means users can take
   advantage of the improved performance of RISC computing. (Note that in a
   WAN implementation, ALL-IN-1 software still requires a VAX system in the
   network to run Message Router for off-system mail delivery. A future
   release of ALL-IN-1 software will remove this restriction.)
o  Users implementing the MAILbus 400 Message Router (XMR) Gateway, also
   being announced in this issue, as their corporate backbone will be able
   to integrate existing ALL-IN-1 systems by use of this XMR gateway.
o  Supports mixed VAX and AXP clusters and mixed DECnet Phase IV and V.
   (Mixed clusters are recommended for WAN implementations.)
o  Re-designed and improved mail server that delivers higher mail throughput
   and now supports the CCITT X.400 standard.
o  Improvements to system management to make managing both VT and PC users
   even easier than before.
o  New features for VT users including mail features, such as blind carbon
   copy, confidentiality, and expiration date indicators, and improvements
   to the file cabinet.
o  A new release of WPS-PLUS for VT users delivers new editor and printing
   features.
o  New interactive TeamLinks server allows interactive ALL-IN-1 script
   processing from a TeamLinks for Windows PC.

New Packaging and Licensing Options

New packaging and licensing options for ALL-IN-1 software provide the
flexibility to insure meeting almost any user's needs. The following
packaging options let users choose the amount of ALL-IN-1 support they want:

o  ALL-IN-1 Integrated Office Server (IOS) -- this is the complete ALL-IN-1
   offering, an integrated office system. It provides VT users with all the
   capabilities provided in ALL-IN-1 software including word processing
   (WPS-PLUS) and time management. This license also supports TeamLinks V2.x
   access to the ALL-IN-1 server.

o  ALL-IN-1 STARTER -- this license includes all the ALL-IN-1 components
   except for time management and customization management capabilities. It
   includes server support for TeamLinks clients.

o  ALL-IN-1 Core Services -- this license includes all the ALL-IN-1
   components except word processing (WPS-PLUS) and time management. It is
   ideal for VT users who need most of the ALL-IN-1 components but plan to
   use other word processors (such as WordPerfect) or scheduling
   applications (such as Calendar Manager). This license also supports
   TeamLinks V2.x access to the ALL-IN-1 server.

o  ALL-IN-1 Client Services Access -- this license provides ALL-IN-1 server
   only access to TeamLinks V2.x clients. It is for TeamLinks V2.x users who
   need to get mail, file cabinet, and directory services from ALL-IN-1
   software (no VT or terminal emulation access is allowed).

This flexibility results in many potential ordering scenarios. So which
ALL-IN-1 package is the right choice? The following table summarizes the
ALL-IN-1 components included with each package:

