       (2) Includes one VT user license for system manager.

Once users decide which ALL-IN-1 components they need, they can now choose
from three different licensing options. The new Concurrent Use license, for
example, reduces the cost of supporting PC and Macintosh clients and
"sometimes connected" VT users. The following licensing options are
available:

o  Traditional -- this license is based on the capacity of the CPU and
   allows the user to run as many users as they wish.

o  Concurrent Use -- this license is purchased on an individual basis and
   allows any user to use the licenses. Concurrent Use supports users on a
   first-come, first-served basis. Once all the Concurrent Use licenses are
   utilized, new user requests for ALL-IN-1 resources will not be honored
   until a license is relinquished by a user exiting ALL-IN-1 software.

o  Personal Use -- this license is also purchased on an individual basis but
   assigned to a specifically named individual user. Any user with a
   Personal Use license is always assured that they will get access to
   ALL-IN-1 software.

BENEFITS

ALL-IN-1 users can now continue to protect investments in OpenVMS
applications while evolving to the next generation Alpha AXP computing
environment. This allows increased computing power and lower cost of
ownership without disrupting mission critical business solutions. Users can
continue to support their VT user population with more modern applications
and improved performance, distribute ALL-IN-1 to smaller workgroups,
including PC LANs, with very small Alpha AXP systems, or do both -- all with
the same ALL-IN-1 software!

ALL-IN-1 software can now meet the demands of PC and Macintosh users to have
a graphical user interface to ALL-IN-1 software, including the ability to
customize existing ALL-IN-1 host-based applications, with a graphical user
interface. And it is easy to install and use -- just add TeamLinks software
to the desktop.

