DECnet/OSI V5.8 for OpenVMS VAX and AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Runs on OpenVMS V6.1 on VAX and AXP systems

o  Provides significant performance and routing enhancement features

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECnet/OSI V5.8 for OpenVMS VAX (SPD 25.03) and OpenVMS AXP (SPD 50.45) is
the latest version of network software based on the Digital Network
Architecture. Phase V of the architecture includes DECnet enhancements and
adds OSI protocol support. The integration of DECnet and OSI enables the use
of both DECnet and OSI applications supported on an OpenVMS platform.

DECnet/OSI preserves existing investments in network hardware and
applications. DECnet/OSI is fully compatible with DECnet Phase IV allowing
existing DECnet applications to run unchanged on a DECnet/OSI system.
DECnet/OSI and DECnet Phase IV systems coexist transparently in a single
network.

DECnet/OSI V5.8 for OpenVMS AXP software adds the following features:

o  Routing segregated mode -- Provides enhanced routing support in networks
   using a combination of Digital and third party dedicated routers by
   allowing the routing layer to choose a Phase IV router for those packets
   having a Phase IV compatible address.

o  Large FDDI packet support -- Supports FDDI packets up to 4,500 bytes to
   deliver increased performance on the network backbone.

o  Reverse path caching --  Provides the ability to track paths through the
   network and remember those paths for future use, improving overall
   network performance.

o  NCL keypad definition -- An example file that may be used for the
   creation of files allowing users to execute commonly used NCL commands
   with one or two keystrokes on the keypad.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECnet/OSI V5.8 for OpenVMS software is available on the consolidated CD-ROM
shipping in September 1994. Pricing is unchanged for this release.

A DECnet/OSI license gives the owner the right to use either DECnet/OSI or
DECnet Phase IV on OpenVMS systems. The DECnet/OSI license frequently is
included as part of VAX and AXP system packages. Users who purchase those
system packages will receive the new V5.8 license. However, a DECnet/OSI
license is not included with all systems. In this case, a new license is
required.

The end system license provides the right to use the base DECnet and OSI
protocol stacks, FTAM, VT, DECdns Clerk, DECdts, X.25 Access, and network
management. The extended function license provides all functions in the end
system plus the OSI application gateways, cluster alias, and, on VAX
platforms, the DECdns server.

Use of the X.25 software to provide direct access to a PSDN (using the
supported WAN device drivers) requires the X.25 license.

Documentation is provided on the CD-ROM. Hard copy documents are also
available. New features for this release are documented in the Release
Notes.

Update Licenses

All DECnet and DECnet/OSI owners must purchase an update license or receive
it as a part of an existing Software Update Subscription License (SUSL)
contract to use V5.8. SUSL is an annual contract that gives the owner rights
to all new releases of software that are released during that year.
Normally, the price is about 12 percent of the new license price per year.
Previous purchase of DECnet or DECnet/OSI software does not convey the right
to use new software versions.

An update license can be obtained by directly purchasing the license (price
is about 30% of new license price) or as part of an existing SUSL contract.

