Forte Curriculum Plan

The curriculum consists of five new classroom based courses and one course
delivered as Computer Based Training.

The courses have been designed to provide three separate tracks:
*  Forte application developers
*  Forte applications designers
*  Forte system managers

The roadmap for these tracks appears below.

Introduction to Forte Distributed Objects (3 hours of CBT)

This introductory course includes key elements of the Forte object oriented
environment. Object oriented programming and distributed objects are
emphasized. Computer Based Training on a PC or Macintosh is the delivery
method.

Forte Concepts and Facilities (1 day)

This course is the prerequisite for all subsequent Forte courses. This
course is designed to introduce the concepts behind Forte distributed
processing, Forte portability and integration issues, the life cycle process
of developing, generating and deploying Forte applications, and an
introduction into the Forte Workshops (development and distribution tools).
Face to face format with lectures and demonstrations is the preferred
delivery method. Additional hands-on exercises are available if the course
is delivered in a classroom with PCs for the students.

Forte Application Development (4 days)

This course provides the application developer with the knowledge needed to
create OO, distributed applications using the unique development features of
Forte. These features include: object oriented language (TOOL),
multiplatform graphical user interface design, multitasking, database
interaction, event handling, exception handling, and transaction handling.
This course also covers the use of the Forte central repository for
application development in a team development environment. It provides the
application developer with the ability to partition and distribute Forte
applications and change the partitioning scheme. Face to face format with
lectures, demonstrations, and hands-on exercises is the preferred delivery
method. The hands-on exercises develop a Forte client/server prototype
application.

Client/Server Application Development with Forte (5 days)

Digital Learning Services also offers Concepts and Facilities and Forte
Application Development as a 5 day course entitled Developing Client/Server
Applications with Forte, EY-M870E-L0. The course content is unchanged.

Forte Advanced Application Development (4 days)

This course provides the Forte application developer with the advanced
knowledge required to program optimized Forte applications and integrate
with existing external routines. The focus is on performance tuning,
optimizing database access, and tips on taking full advantage of additional
technical features within the Forte product such as casting, nested windows,
and implementation of complex transaction management. This course also
covers partitioning schemes to address fault tolerance and load balancing.
Face to face format with lectures, demonstrations, and hands-on exercises is
the preferred delivery method. The hands-on exercises enhance a Forte
client/server prototype application. Students should have at least six weeks
of Forte application development experience before commencing this course.

Forte Application Design (5 days)

This course provides MIS professionals who will be designing Forte
applications with the knowledge needed to create a robust and comprehensive
object oriented design that will maximize reusability and high performance
for Forte applications. It will include learning an object oriented analysis
and design method. This course also covers detailed sessions on Forte
specific design techniques to leverage the distribution of Forte
client/server applications. Lectures and demonstrations comprise the format.

Forte System Management (3 days)

This course covers all aspects of Forte system management, including
installation, day to day operation, software maintenance, and environment
setup. Lectures and demonstrations comprise the format.

