OpenVMS Management Station V1.0 for OpenVMS VAX

HIGHLIGHTS

o  New PC based Management Station provides graphical user interface for
   managing one or more OpenVMS clusters from a single point

o  Based on PATHWORKS ManageWORKS which affords a hierarchical system view

o  Contains the infrastructure and the implementation of user account
   management

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The OpenVMS Management Station V1.0 enables management of one or more
OpenVMS Cluster systems from a single Windows based PC. This is the model
for OpenVMS system management for the future.

The Management Station software is based on the PATHWORKS V5.0A ManageWORKS
framework. This graphical user interface provides the infrastructure for
implementation of system management functions such as user account
management. The ManageWORKS framework presents a hierarchical management
view and provides the ability to manage multiple OpenVMS systems from a
single source. It enables users to view, organize, and manage objects in a
way that is meaningful to them. The interface provides an integrated,
consistent look-and-feel for all OpenVMS management tools as opposed to the
varied syntax of the DCL interface for each utility today.

The Management Station is geared to OpenVMS multicluster sites -- in
particular environments consisting of PC LANs with OpenVMS hosts. While the
Management Station is intended to manage only the OpenVMS environment (it is
not intended to be an enterprise director), the ManageWORKS interface
provides the opportunity for integration of applications and services for
both LAN and OpenVMS management under one framework. V1.0 of the Management
Station focuses on user account management, while other functional areas
will be implemented in subsequent versions.

The Management Station is comprised of a client and a server component. The
Windows based client is installed on a PC and is the point from which all
operations are performed. The PC must also have the PATHWORKS V5.0A client
installed. The Management Station server component must be installed on all
of the OpenVMS systems to be managed. The PATHWORKS server is not required.

The product uses domains to group systems into a management hierarchy. A
domain is any system or collection of systems to be managed as one unit. The
contents of a domain might be some of the OpenVMS Clusters in a network, all
the systems in a building, or only the systems on one floor of a
building. Within the hierarchy of domains, the scope of an operation is the
set of systems on which the operation takes place. For example, the scope of
an operation such as account creation or deletion might be a single system
or every system in the environment.

The Management Station provides the ability to perform operations across
multiple systems. For example, assume that a user has an account on several
different OpenVMS Cluster systems and that a particular attribute, such as
disk quota, needs to be modified. Using the Management Station, the
attribute can easily be modified for each instance of the user account in a
single operation.

This product also provides a comprehensive interface for user account
management. Account creation has traditionally included the following steps:
o  Adding a UAF entry.
o  Granting rights identifiers.
o  Creating a directory.
o  Creating disk quotas.
o  Creating a mail profile.

All the above steps are now handled through the Management Station
interface, eliminating the need to use several utilities and DCL. In
addition, the Management Station also allows creation of network proxy
records. A new feature is support for storing personal information such as
phone number, location, and site-specific identification.

The Management Station supports the following account management operations:
o  Create user accounts.
o  Modify account characteristics (any aspect).
o  Delete user accounts.
o  Rename user accounts.
o  Display user account attributes.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

OpenVMS Management Station V1.0 for OpenVMS VAX software is available now
through the DECdirect service, local Digital sales offices, and Digital's
business partners.

The Management Station software is licensed and supported under the OpenVMS
license and will be included with the next operating system release for VAX
and AXP platforms. The kit being released at this time is for OpenVMS VAX
software. It includes:

o  1 TK50
o  2 PC floppy disks
o  OpenVMS Management Station Installation Guide -- AA-Q9AYA-TE
o  OpenVMS Management Station Overview and Release Notes -- AA-Q9B0A-TE
o  OpenVMS Management Station Cover Letter -- AA-Q9AZA-TE

Order No.        Description

