PREREQUISITES

Software for OpenVMS Management Station V1.0

o  The Management Station is designed as a client/server application. Any
   OpenVMS nonclustered node or OpenVMS Cluster system to be managed must be
   running OpenVMS VAX V6.1.

o  The PC client requires Windows V3.1 or Windows for Workgroups V3.11 and
   PATHWORKS client V5.0A. NOTE: The PATHWORKS client MUST be V5.0A; it may
   not be either V5.0 or any subsequent version to V5.0A. Also note that the
   PATHWORKS server is not required.

TECHNICAL DATA

Restrictions

o  Managing OpenVMS cluster members as individual nodes is not supported.
   OpenVMS cluster systems are treated as indivisible entities; an operation
   cannot be performed on particular cluster members.

o  V1.0 can be used in a mixed-architecture cluster with both VAX and AXP
   systems present but only the OpenVMS VAX nodes can run the Management
   Station server.

o  Creating nodes in an OpenVMS cluster or deleting them from an OpenVMS
   cluster is not supported.

o  OpenVMS Clusters with multiple user authorization files (UAFs) are not
   supported.

o  DECnet Phase IV is the only supported network transport from the PC.
   OpenVMS Management Station does support use of DECnet Phase V between
   servers that use Phase IV alias names.

