POLYCENTER System Watchdog V2.2

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Event monitoring and notification on multiple platforms

o  V2.2 extends support from OpenVMS VAX and ULTRIX RISC systems to include
   OpenVMS AXP, DEC OSF/1, HP-UX, SunOS, and AIX platforms

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

POLYCENTER System Watchdog (SPD #41.42.03) is a distributed software
application that monitors system and subsystem events, notifies personnel of
problems, and automatically issues pre-programmed responses to counter the
impact of the events. The System Watchdog is an important solution for the
multivendor enterprise to expedite the goal of centralized problem
management, while at the same time cut cost and operating expenses through
timely responses, automation, and a client/server architecture.

POLYCENTER System Watchdog comes in two components, which may reside on the
same or different systems/supported platforms:

o  Server (also known as the Consolidator) -- consolidates event information
   generated from agents and applies the proper notification and action
   responses. It is supported on OpenVMS, DEC OSF/1 AXP, and ULTRIX
   platforms.

o  Agent -- monitors system, subsystem, and device events on the residence
   node. It is supported on OpenVMS VAX or AXP, DEC OSF/1 AXP, HP-UX, SunOS,
   AIX, and ULTRIX platforms.

BENEFITS

POLYCENTER System Watchdog significantly improves datacenter productivity
by:

o  Providing timely and reliable monitoring and notification of system
   events.

o  Centralizing problem management across the network and multivendor
   platforms.

o  Automating responsive actions to events to reduce cost of time and
   processes lost to failures.

