COHESION Team/SEE V1.1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Digital's CASE Software Engineering Environment (SEE) and services for
   UNIX updated with new features and capabilities

o  Built upon COHESIONworX foundation, focuses on improving the software
   development practices of large application development teams

o  DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.0, SunOS V4.1.3, and HP-UX V9.03 platform support

o  Additional support for Teamwork, Interleaf, PCMS, RTM, and StP/OMT

o  Integration support for Digital Tool's AutoPLAN II and Frame Technology's
   FrameMaker

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The COHESION Team/SEE product is a set of software tools and consulting
services for managing data and development processes for
medium-to-large-scale UNIX software engineering projects distributed across
multivendor, multisite environments. It is intended to enhance the
efficiency of large software development teams and to improve software
product reliability. The COHESION Team/SEE product supports the
Carnegie-Mellon Software Engineering Institute Capability and Maturity Model
(SEI-CMM) Level III efficiency model for process support and workflow
control.

The COHESION Team/SEE product provides the base environment to support the
full software development lifecycle. The prerequisite Digital COHESIONworX
product (see the COHESIONworX V2.1 article in this issue) provides the
underlying desktop, software development tools, control services, and
integration capabilities. The COHESION Team/SEE product consists of a number
of software applications that provide a minimum viable system. An additional
set of applications may be added as options to the environment in order to
provide enhanced capability.

Each option listed below is delivered with a Team/SEE EnCASEment, which
integrates the application into the Team/SEE environment. The COHESION
Team/SEE product optionally includes:

o  Requirements Management, based on Marconi Systems Technology's
   Requirements and Traceability Management (RTM).

o  Software Analysis and Design, based on Cadre Technologies' Teamwork.

o  Software Analysis and Design, based on Interactive Development
   Environments Inc's Software through Pictures/Object Modeling Technique
   (StP/OMT).

o  Software Metrics Collection and Reporting, based on Amadeus Software
   Research Inc's Amadeus Measurement System.

o  Technical Documentation, based on Interleaf Inc.'s Interleaf 6 for Motif.

COHESION Team/SEE also supports another set of options available for
purchase from the appropriate vendor. Digital maintains a Team/SEE
EnCASEment for each option that integrates the application into the Team/SEE
environment:

o  Team/SEE EnCASEment for Digital Tool's AutoPLAN II.
o  Team/SEE EnCASEment for Frame Technology's FrameMaker.

COHESION Team/SEE V1.1 Enhancements

The COHESION Team/SEE V1.1 product has been enhanced to operate using DEC
OSF/1 V2.0 software (SPD 50.85), with expected upwards compatibility with
DEC OSF/1 V2.1 software. The HP-UX V9.03 (SPD 50.87) operating system
support has also been added. This is in addition to supporting the SunOS
V4.1.3 (SPD 50.86) operating system. The execution of any software
application integrated into the COHESION Team/SEE V1.1 product or
COHESIONWorX V2.1 software is supported on any supported hardware platform
and operating system. For example, COHESION Team/SEE V1.1 on a DEC OSF/1 AXP
platform has the ability to execute applications transparently that operate
on SunOS or HP-UX systems.

V1.1 also adds support for a number of applications integrated into the
overall environment. This includes:

o  The latest version of SQL Software's PCMS, which provides the core
   configuration management capability for the COHESION Team/SEE product.
   Many enhancements are provided in this release of PCMS, along with an
   Application Programming Interface (API) that has allowed an even tighter
   integration of PCMS into COHESION Team/SEE environment.

o  Support for Cadre's Teamwork on OSF/1 has been added, in addition to
   existing integrations for Teamwork on SunOS and HP-UX.

o  Support for Interleaf's Interleaf 6 for Motif on SunOS has been added, in
   addition to existing integrations for Interleaf 6 on OSF/1 and HP-UX.

o  Support for Marconi's RTM on OSF/1 has been added, in addition to
   existing integrations for RTM on SunOS and HP-UX.

o  An IDE StP/OMT integration is now available on OSF/1, SunOS, and HP-UX
   platforms, integrating StP/OMT into the Team/SEE environment.

o  A Digital Tool AutoPLAN II integration is now available on OSF/1, SunOS,
   and HP-UX platforms, integrating AutoPLAN II into the Team/SEE
   environment. Note that AutoPLAN II is purchased directly from Digital
   Tools.

o  A Frame Technology FrameMaker integration is now available on SunOS and
   HP-UX platforms, integrating FrameMaker into the Team/SEE environment.
   Note that FrameMaker is purchased directly from Digital Tools.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The COHESION Team/SEE V1.1 product is available now. Pricing is based on a
core package of common software, with incremental pricing for a selection of
Digital and third-party applications. COHESION Team/SEE media and
documentation are sold separately.

The COHESION Team/SEE product requires certain software pre-requisites. When
configuring a COHESION Team/SEE system, refer to the applicable platform SPD
for software and hardware requirements.

Team/SEE EnCASEments (TSE)

A TSE is Digital's added-value integration component that allows COHESION
Team/SEE supported optional products to be integrated immediately into both
the COHESION Team/SEE and COHESIONworX environments. When purchased from
Digital, each product option includes a license to use the TSE for that
product. COHESION Team/SEE supported products not purchased from Digital may
