DEC Ada V3.2 for DEC OSF/1 AXP V3.0 Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Enhanced DEC Ada features for DEC OSF/1 AXP V3.0 systems

o  Symmetric multiprocessing (SMP) support and passive tasking

o  DEC Ada Professional Development Option for DEC OSF/1 systems now
   includes Quick Link

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DEC Ada is Digital's validated implementation of the full
ANSI/MIL-STD-1815A-1983 Ada language. As a result of meeting the ANSI
standard, DEC Ada also conforms to the Federal Information Processing
Standard (FIPS-119) and the International Standards Organization
(ISO/8652-1987) standards for the Ada programming language.

DEC Ada provides a modular structure for programs by allowing separate
compilation of program units, as well as providing strong typing, tasking,
exception handling, and other standard language features that are supported
across implementations. DEC Ada V3.2 provides highly optimized code running
on DEC OSF/1 AXP V3.0 (SPD 41.61) systems. It also provides a number of
features that make it suitable for a variety of applications -- from general
systems to realtime applications.

Compiler Features

o  Support for running DEC Ada tasks within the same program on multiple
   processors. DEC Ada multitasking applications automatically take
   advantage of symmetric multiprocessing (SMP) when running on a DEC OSF/1
   system that supports SMP.

o  Support for the POSIX Ada Language Interface bindings as required by IEEE
   Standard 1003.5.

o  Support for the ISO Math Library packages GENERIC_PRIMITIVE_FUNCT and
   GENERIC_ELEMENTARY_FUNCTIONS.

o  Support for passive tasks that can significantly improve the performance
   of rendezvous in programs.

o  Improved debugging capabilities and new DECladebug support.

Professional Development Option

The DEC Ada Professional Development Option is a separately licensed option
that is available with DEC Ada for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems. Ada programmers do
not need to change any of their development procedures to benefit from the
DEC Ada Professional Development Option. This option includes:

o  Smart Recompilation -- Significantly reduces the number of recompilations
   that are needed to rebuild a DEC Ada program after compilation units have
   changed; eliminates up to 100 percent of the usual recompilations.

o  Program Library File-Block Caching -- Minimizes the actual amount of disk
   I/O that must be performed by using an in-memory cache of file blocks.
   The elapsed time for compilations is significantly reduced.

o  Quick Link -- Significantly reduces, during incremental program
   development, the time to relink a large DEC Ada program after changes to
   a small number of program units.

DEC FUSE V2.0 Ada Support

DEC FUSE Ada Support for DEC OSF/1 AXP (SPD 44.71) provides special support
features for programmers using DEC Ada for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems. DEC FUSE
for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems is Digital's integrated development environment
for UNIX developers. DEC FUSE provides a graphical user interface to
Digital's DEC OSF/1 compilers and is a major element of the COHESION
product.

The primary benefit for DEC Ada users is the graphical programming
environment provided by the DEC FUSE integrated development tools that
support DEC Ada for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems. DEC FUSE Ada support provides the
ability for programmers to view an Ada application structure graphically
during the development cycle. This visual capability makes it easier to
navigate through complex programs and provides a smoother flow to problem
solving, which greatly simplifies and reduces errors and increases
programmer productivity.

BENEFITS

DEC Ada enables software developers to create high quality applications
quickly and efficiently within a comprehensive development environment. As a
native mode language, it is also well integrated with the services and
utilities available on the following systems: DEC OSF/1 AXP, OpenVMS AXP,
and OpenVMS VAX systems.

DEC Ada V3.2 continues to provide a highly reliable, standards based,
quality Ada compilation system based on the well-known DEC Ada product for
OpenVMS systems. By remaining true to the Ada language standard, DEC Ada
V3.2 provides the same look and feel across multiple platforms and maintains
a high degree of application portability.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING INFORMATION

DEC Ada V3.2 for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems is available now through local
Digital sales offices and the DECdirect service.

The QA-0VSAA-GZ Read Before Installation Letter must be ordered (at no cost)
with all licenses for DEC Ada Professional Development Option for DEC OSF/1
AXP systems.

The DEC Ada Professional Development Option for DEC OSF/1 AXP Systems
binaries are provided with the DEC Ada binaries on the Layered Product
CD-ROM. Purchase of a DEC Ada Professional Development Option for DEC OSF/1
AXP systems license (QL-0VSA*-**) enables use of this capability.

Documentation for the DEC Ada Professional Development Option is provided in
Chapter 5 of Developing Ada Programs on DEC OSF/1 Systems.

