DCE V1.1 for Windows NT

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Provides DCE server capability on Windows NT platform

o  Interoperates with DCE compliant clients running on any vendor's platform

o  Fully compliant with the OSF DCE server specifications

o  Includes a graphical DCE management tool that greatly simplifies the
   management of a DCE environment

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DCE (Distributed Computing Environment) V1.1 for Windows NT product (SPD
53.43) provides the Windows NT implementation of the distributed computing
functionality specified by the Open Software Foundation (OSF). It allows
users to deploy the DCE Servers (Cell Directory Server and the DCE Security
Server) on the Windows NT platform.

The DCE is a comprehensive, integrated set of services and tools that
support the creation, use, and maintenance of client/server applications in
heterogeneous, multivendor environments. Application programmers can now
design and build a client/server application that runs over a variety of
operating systems and networks. Programmers simply code to the DCE Remote
Procedure Call using a set of standardized APIs to reap the benefits of all
the underlying DCE components. The DCE also masks from the application
programmer the complexities and differences between the underlying network,
operating systems, and hardware platforms. The programmer no longer needs to
be concerned with data types or networking schemes. The DCE makes those
network elements transparent to the programmer and helps make multivendor
interoperability and application portability a reality.

New features of this version of the DCE product include:

o  DCE Security Server -- Provides secure communications and access via
   authorization and authentication services.

o  DCE Cell Directory Service (CDS) -- Provides location independent naming
   for resources.

o  DCE Manager -- An intuitive, easy-to-learn graphical tool for the
   management of a DCE environment; allows management tasks (such as
   creation and control of ACLs, CDS directories, user accounts, and user
   groups) to be done easily.

o  Upgrade to the OSF DCE V1.0.3 source base.

BENEFITS

o  Gives system managers greater flexibility in designing and configuring
   their DCE environments.

o  Provides a robust, scalable Directory and Security Service, which can
   provide the naming and security services for large DCE environments.

o  Provides full interoperability with DCE clients running on any vendor
   platform.

o  Simplifies management of the DCE environment.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Digital DCE V1.1 for Windows NT product is available now both as a
layered product and as part of the PATHWORKS product set. It is orderable
through the DECdirect service. The DCE Manager utility is included as part
of the DCE Runtime Services kit.

