DEC TCP/IP Services V3.2 for OpenVMS VAX and AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Network File System (NFS) Client

o  Anonymous file transfer protocol

o  Token ring support for the OpenVMS AXP platform

o  Runs on OpenVMS VAX and AXP V6.0 and V6.1

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS VAX and AXP software provides OpenVMS users with
the ability to share resources among all their information processing
resources, from OpenVMS environments to UNIX to PCs, running the TCP/IP and
NFS protocols. The product provides for all major applications such as file
transfer, mail, remote login, NFS file systems, TCP/IP naming services and
management (BIND and SNMP), multiple programming interfaces including
SUNrpc, and robust printing resources, including remote printing via TELNET.

The new features of DEC TCP/IP Services V3.2 include:

o  NFS Client -- The Network File System protocol allows users to remotely
   access a host file system as if it were the user's local file system. DEC
   TCP/IP Services has always shipped the NFS Server, allowing UNIX users to
   mount OpenVMS files as if they were local UNIX files. Now, with V3.2 of
   DEC TCP/IP Services, OpenVMS users can mount NFS files stored on other
   hosts as if they were local OpenVMS files. Users can execute all major
   file activities such as create/delete, read/write, and set attributes.

o  Anonymous FTP -- Anonymous FTP is used to make information public and
   easily available on an internetwork. It allows remote users, without an
   account on a specific node, to copy files to and from that node. Access
   is usually achieved by providing the user name "anonymous," and the
   password "guest." Anonymous FTP has become increasingly popular as a
   means to distribute various corporate resources from patches to software,
   to update product literature via the public Internet. It can be used on
   any network, including private ones, as long as the TCP/IP protocol is
   present. System managers must take care to restrict access to specific
   files or areas, and further prohibit backdoor security leaks.

o  Token Ring for OpenVMS AXP platform -- With token ring being the
   principal LAN alternative to Ethernet, the addition of token ring support
   allows OpenVMS AXP machines to participate in a TCP/IP based, token ring
   client/server environment.

AVAILABILITY and ORDERING

DEC TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS VAX and AXP software will be available in
October 1994. The OpenVMS VAX version will be available on the consolidated
CD-ROM, as well as TK50s and magtape. The OpenVMS AXP version will be
available via the AXP CD-ROM Software Library Program. Hard copy
documentation is also available for both platforms.

Users can purchase the entire product, DEC TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS VAX
and AXP software, or a client license only --  DEC TCP/IP Client for OpenVMS
VAX and AXP software. There is also an upgrade license path, from client to
server, via the license -- DEC TCP/IP Client Upgrade for OpenVMS VAX and AXP
software.

Additionally, the product is available in all NAS OpenVMS packages. Check
the NAS package descriptions to ensure purchase of the entire product or the
client license only.

DEC TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS VAX and AXP software can be purchased as a
Traditional Unlimited Capacity license. Most users purchase the entire
product, DEC TCP/IP Services, which gives them license rights to use all
functionality, including the new components.

Beginning with the V3.0 of this product, a new cost effective client only
license was implemented. The client license (DEC TCP/IP Client for OpenVMS
VAX and AXP license) does not include the license rights to the NFS Server,
the BIND Server, or to the Remote Boot Server. It is a traditional client
license, priced at 50 percent below the full function license, making it an
attractive workstation, or low end CPU license, and it includes license
rights to the new NFS Client at no additional cost.

If a user wishes to upgrade from a client license to the entire product, an
upgrade license, DEC TCP/IP Client Upgrade for OpenVMS VAX and AXP software,
is available for the exact cost difference between the two licenses.

