Remote users with notebooks can also access either the PSTN using a PCMCIA
asynchronous modem or the PSDN network using a PCMCIA synchronous modem and
the X.32 service offered in many countries. The X.32 service is an extension
of the PSDN that allows access via a normal dial-up telephone line (PSTN).
This solution adds the dimension of mobility for PATHWORKS Remote users.

When selecting ISDN connectivity PATHWORKS Remote enables a user to connect
a single PATHWORKS PC client to the ISDN Basic Rate Access and provides a
TCP/IP or DECnet link by using either PPP or X.25 over one B-channel. A new,
Windows based, Connection Manager application includes a connection diary
that provides the user a simple graphic user interface for configuring
different connections, connecting and disconnecting, and managing a database
of all connection choices.

