   PC boards distributed by Digital, cable, and an ISDN PCSO controller
   card.
o  For desktop PC and notebook PC connected to the PSTN running asynchronous
   communication, you need any PTT certified modem, the PSTN running
   synchronous communication and accessing the PSDN, and an external X.32
   pocket modem (e.g., Microspeedy or Pocket32).
o  Software includes all required drivers to support ISDN, X.25 PC cards,
   and X.32 modems.
o  ISDN:
   - Basic Rate Access that supports CCITT I430/40/50/51 recommendations.
   - ISA card distributed by Digital for desktop PCs.
o  PSDN (X.25):
   - Meets CCITT X.25 1984 & 1988 recommendations, with more than 80
     different PSDN profiles already configured.
   - ISA and MCA X.25 cards distributed by Digital for Desktop PCs.
o  X.32 (dial-in to the PSDN):
   - Service available in Europe in more than 13 countries.
   - X.32 runs with one PCMCIA V2.0 (up to 14.4 bp/s) autosync modem.
   - X.32 runs with external autosync modem connected to the COM port.
o  PSTN (dial-in async):
   - Support Hayes/V25 modems connected to the COM port.
   - PCMCIA asynchrounous modem.
   - DDCMP or SLIP or IP over PPP.

