 ..................... A N N O U N C E M E N T S ......................

 DIGITAL AND ORACLE MAKE PROVISIONS FOR Rdb PRODUCTS UNDER THE CSLG AND
 DECCAMPUS PROGRAMS....Digital and Oracle have announced a new strategic
 alliance with Oracle acquiring Digital's Rdb database, DBA Workcenter,
 and repository businesses. When the acquisition becomes effective,
 educational institutions in the CSLG or DECcampus Program will continue
 to receive campuswide licenses for "the Rdb Products" in the Programs,
 but they will be "locked" at the current version. This will allow
 customers to plan, budget and transition to Oracle's Education Program
 for updates, new versions and service. Products used in an academic
 environment should see little change, and products used in an
 administration environment will be available with education discounts
 that are consistent with the education industry. Digital will continue
 to be responsible for all existing Education Software Library (ESL)
 maintenance contracts that support the Rdb Products until each annual
 contract expires.

 For additional information, contact Oracle at 1-800-ORACLE1 in the U.S.
 or 1-415-506-5701 outside the U.S. Or, contact Digital at 1-800-DIGITAL
 in the U.S., 353-91-754-567 in Europe, and internationally via FAX
 603-881-1868, or via electronic mail to TEIHOTLINE@ako.mts.dec.com.

 * Digital and Oracle "Announcement-At-A-Glance" and Press Release;
   news1001.txt;

 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW GENERATION OF WORLD'S FASTEST ALPHA AXP MICRO-
 PROCESSORS......Digital has announced the world's fastest and highest-
 performance microprocessor for both server and client systems, the
 Alpha AXP 21164-300MHz and Alpha AXP 21164-266MHz. First in a new
 generation of Alpha AXP microprocessors, the chip is the first to reach
 or exceed one billion instructions per second (BIPS). The AXP micro-
 processors are ideally suited for server applications involving
 multiple databases, groupware for departments and workgroups, and high-
 volume transaction processing. They also offer the industry's fastest
 execution of demanding client applications, such as mechanical and
 electronic computer-aided design (CAD), computer-assisted software
 engineering (CASE), high-performance graphics and imaging, multimedia,
 voice recognition, and scientific and financial analysis.

 * Press Release - New Alpha AXP MicroProcessors; news1002.txt;

 DIGITAL ADDS ALPHA AXP SUPPORT FOR FIVE MILLION ALL-IN-1 USERS.....
 Digital has announced the availability of the world's most widely used
 integrated office software -- ALL-IN-1 Office Server software -- on
 Alpha AXP systems running the OpenVMS operating system. Alpha AXP
 support increases performance, lowers cost of ownership and protects
 the investments of current ALL-IN-1 users. The office groupware now
 runs on Alpha AXP and VAX servers running the OpenVMS operating system
 and supports networked terminals, PCs, and Macintosh computers across
 widely distributed enterprise networks. ALL-IN-1 software includes
 enterprise groupware applications and services such as mail, shared
 filing, conferencing, word processing, group scheduling, system
 management and administration.

 * Info Sheet - All-in-1 Office Server OpenVMS AXP; news1003.txt;

 DECUS U.S. CHAPTER LAUNCHES ITS WORLD WIDE WEB SERVER.......The U.S.
 Chapter of DECUS, the Digital Equipment Computer Users Society, has
 announced the activation of its World Wide Web information server. The
 server, which can be accessed at URL http://www.decus.org/, allows
 members, utilizing a Web browser such as Mosaic, access to graphically
 enhanced hypertext files containing information on: the products and
 services of the Chapter; the structure of U.S. Chapter organization;
 the DECUS/Digital relationship; and more. The server also allows
 readers to apply for membership in the Chapter via an on-line
 application form, and to "link" to other information servers including
 those operated by Digital Equipment Corporation and various DECUS
 chapters from around the world. The server provides easy and immediate
 access to the upcoming DECUS '94/Anaheim program information including
 sessions and seminars abstracts, event highlights and updates, a list
 of trade show vendors, and registration and hotel information.

 * Press Release - DECUS Announces World Wide Web Server; news1004.txt;

 DIGITAL AND PROCESS SOFTWARE SIGN JOINT TCP/IP TECHNOLOGY AGREEMENT....
 Digital and Process Software Corporation have announced a long-term
 joint technology agreement designed to deliver new TCP/IP solutions to
 OpenVMS users. Under the agreement, Process Software will license
 elements of its product, TCPware, to Digital. TCPware is a complete
 TCP/IP networking solution for Digital OpenVMS VAX and Alpha AXP
 systems that integrates these systems into heterogeneous networks.
 Digital will integrate these new features into its TCP/IP Services for
 OpenVMS product to offer customers a richer TCP/IP environment, with
 release of the next version of the product planned for this fall. The
 long-term goal of the agreement is the development of a single unified
 product that offers the best TCP/IP solution on OpenVMS platforms. In
 the interim, both companies will continue to enhance their individual
 offerings. The terms of the agreement allow for the TCP/IP products to
 remain under the CSLG and DECcampus programs.

 * Press Release - Digital and Process Software; news1005.txt

 COEXISTENCE TOOLS FOR OPENVMS PACKAGED WITH DEC OSF/1........Six key
 tools for interoperability and coexistence with OpenVMS computing
 environments will be included at no charge with the latest version of
 the DEC OSF/1 operating system. The suite of interoperability tools,
 supplied under a contract between Digital, Sector 7, and Boston
 Business Computing, Ltd., Inc. include EDT+, Vmail, VX/DCL, VX/JSP,
 VCL, and Vbackup. The tools, provided at no charge, on the new compact
 disk make editing, mail, command line, job and print queue, and backup
 functions identical between UNIX systems and existing Digital systems
 running the OpenVMS operating system. Users, programmers, and
 administrators working in mixed environments are presented with a
 consistent environment.

 OBJECTSTORE TO BE AVAILABLE ON ALPHA AXP.......Digital has announced a
 strategic relationship with Object Design, Inc. that will make Object-
 Store, the industry's leading object database management system,
 available on Digital's DEC OSF/1 and OpenVMS platforms. ObjectStore is
 used in very technically demanding applications and the Alpha AXP
 platform provides the address space, performance, and scalability
 customers need for object oriented applications. ObjectStore features
 distribution and transaction management for concurrent access to
 objects among members of a workgroup, and offers state-of-the-art
 database functions such as data integrity, version control, and query
 processing.

 * Press Release - Digital and Object Design, Inc.; news1006.txt;

 ENTERPRISE MANAGEMENT APPLICATION MOVES TO ALPHA AXP PLATFORM......
 Saros Corporation, a leading enterprise library services provider for
 customers currently on LANs or moving applications off mainframes, has
 announced it will port Saros Mezzanine enterprise management technology
 to the Alpha AXP platform running both the DEC OSF/1 and Windows NT
 operating systems. This supports the growing number of Digital
 customers downsizing from outdated mainframe technologies. Availability
 on DEC OSF/1 is planned for October 1994; availability on Windows NT is
 planned for later in the calendar year. Upon availability for shipment,
 Digital plans to become a reseller for both versions.

 .........................E V E N T S ..................................

 DIGITAL TO EXHIBIT AT EDUCOM CONFERENCE......The EDUCOM Conference is
 the largest and most important meeting on information technology
 policy, trends, and applications in higher education. The programs at
 the conference are primarily focused on networking and integrating
 information technology into the campus and curriculum. Digital will be
 exhibiting innovative solutions and services that meet the Internet
 technology needs of customers and partners at the upcoming EDUCOM
 Conference. Some of these exhibits include:

   *  Alpha-AXP based Internet servers
   *  Mosaic Internet navigation software for Internet
      navigation, browsing, and Home Page creation
   *  Use of the Internet as a channel for direct purchases
      through Digital's Electronic Connection
   *  The Alpha AXP Internet program enabling Internet users
      to test drive Alpha AXP systems for free

      Event:       EDUCOM Conference
      Date:        October 31 - November 3, 1994
      Place:       San Antonio Convention Center
                   San Antonio, TX, U.S.A.

 DIGITAL TO PARTICIPATE IN MATERIALS RESEARCH SOCIETY MEETING....Digital
 will have a booth (#912) located in University Hall of the Boston
 Marriott featuring Alpha AXP workstations running two modeling
 demonstrations: Schrodinger Inc.'s PS-GVB, a quantum mechanics code
 originally developed in the labs of Richard Friesner and William
 Goddard,III; and Waterloo Maple Inc. Maple V software, a mathematical
 modeling tool for researchers developing their own applications. Come
 by to view these demonstrations and to get an update on our latest
 products and applications.

   Event:          Materials Research Society Meeting
   Date:           November 29 - December 1, 1994,
   Place:          Marriott Hotel, Boston, MA

 DIGITAL TO SPONSOR INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON COMPUTER MANAGED
 LEARNING (CML).......CML'94 will provide an international forum for the
 exchange of ideas and information about the introduction, application
 and use of Computer Managed Learning supporting education and training
 strategies, both on-site and at a distance, through remote dial-in
 access. The conference theme is "The Cost Effective Management of
 Learning" and the program will explore how CML can improve the quality,
 productivity, and accessibility of education and training. Digital and
 Campus America are major sponsors of the conference. The conference
 will be of interest to lecturers, teachers, providers of support
 services, administrators and policy makers in universities, community
 colleges, polytechnics, schools, governments and industry.

      Event:       Computer Managed Learning (CML)
      Date:        December 5-9, 1994
      Place:       Melbourne, Australia

 * For more details contact The Meeting Planners: phone (613)819-3700,
   fax (613)819-5978, e-mail CML94@RMIT.edu.au

 ................... C U S T O M E R  N E W S .........................

 ALPHA AXP SYSTEMS SUCCESSFULLY SUPPORTS INTERNATIONAL BROADCAST OVER
 THE MBONE.......Two Alpha AXP workstations successfully supported the
 International Conference on Intelligent Systems for Molecular Biology
 (ISMB), held recently at Stanford University. The Alpha AXP systems
 were used to broadcast the conference over the internet multimedia
 backbone (MBONE). Using the AXP systems, Dan Mosedale, the MBONE
 coordinator, was able to set up a broadcast of two images (one of the
 speaker and one of the speaker's slides) and voice of the speaker, as
 well as a common area "whiteboard" that allowed watchers to provide
 side comments on what was happening. "The Alphas functioned flawlessly,
 and handled the broadcast with no problem" said Russ Altman of the
 ISMB-94 Organizing Committee. "It was clearly a leading edge technol-
 ogy, and we were all happy to participate in the first molecular
 biology conference to be broadcast in its entirety." At any given time,
 there were 20-30 viewers around the world viewing the broadcast,
 including Sweden, Australia, the United Kingdom, Europe, and many of
 the U.S. Department of Energy Laboratories (Argonne, Los Alamos,
 Oakridge).

 * Contact: Russ B. Altman, MD, PhD; Assistant Professor of Medicine
   Section on Medical Informatics; Stanford University; ISMB-94
   Organizing Committee; altman@camis.Stanford.EDU

