DECUS World Wide Web Server Press Release

 DECUS U.S. CHAPTER ANNOUNCES LAUNCH OF WORLD WIDE WEB SERVER

        Current postings include public domain library programs,
               information on DECUS '94/Anaheim, and more

 SHREWSBURY, MA, September 26, 1994 -- The U.S. Chapter of DECUS, the
 Digital Equipment Computer Users Society, this week announced the
 activation of its World Wide Web information server. The server, which
 can be accessed at URL http://www.decus.org/, represents the most
 recent of the Chapter's efforts to provide channels of communication
 which contribute to the success of its membership.

 Utilizing a Web browser such as Mosaic, readers of the server may
 access graphically enhanced hypertext files containing information on:
 the products and services of the Chapter; the structure of U.S. Chapter
 organization; the DECUS/Digital relationship; and more. The server also
 allows readers to apply for membership in the Chapter via an on-line
 application form, and to "link" to other information servers including
 those operated by Digital Equipment Corporation and various DECUS
 chapters from around the world.

 The activation of the DECUS U.S. Chapter Web server coincides with the
 release of information on DECUS '94/Anaheim, the organization's
 seminars, symposium, and trade show event scheduled for December 10-15.
 The server provides easy and immediate access to DECUS '94/Anaheim
 program information including: sessions and seminars abstracts; event
 highlights and updates; a listing of trade show vendors; as well as
 registration and hotel information. Registration and hotel forms will
 also be posted in GIF file format which readers may transfer to a
 client system for printing.

 The server is also slated to become the new home of the DECUS Public
 Domain Software Library. Moving the Library to the server allows
 readers to access, review, and pull down any and all available software
 programs they need, all for the cost of their Internet connection.
 Close to 45 percent of all current DECUS Library programs have already
 been loaded onto the server, including nearly 90 percent of all
 available OpenVMS software programs. Plans call for moving the majority
 of the DECUS Library programs onto the Web server within a year.

 Long-range plans call for additional communications tools and
 information resources to be made available through the DECUS U.S.
 Chapter Web server including: expanded conferencing capabilities;
 on-line product demonstrations; beta test information; and the addition
 of industry-wide technology repository files.

 The U.S. Chapter of DECUS, the Digital Equipment Computer Users
 Society, is an association of Information Technology professionals
 interested in the products, services, and technologies of Digital
 Equipment Corporation and related vendors. The Association's purpose is
 to promote the unimpeded exchange of information, with the goal of
 helping its members and their organizations to be more successful. The
 Chapter provides each member with means to enhance their professional
 development, forums for technical training, mechanisms for obtaining
 up-to-date information, advocacy programs, and opportunities for
 informal disclosure and interaction with professional colleagues of
 like interests.

                                     ####

 DECUS, the DECUS logo, Digital, and OpenVMS are trademarks of Digital
 Equipment Corporation.



