Digital and Object Design, Inc. Press Release

 DIGITAL INKS AGREEMENT WITH OBJECT DESIGN, INC.

 ObjectStore for DEC OSF/1 and OpenVMS Platforms

 MAYNARD, MA -- September 6, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation today
 announced a strategic relationship with Object Design, Inc. that will
 include engineering exchanges and joint marketing programs. As an
 initial step, ObjectStore, the industry's leading object database
 management system, will be made available on Digital's DEC OSF/1 and
 OpenVMS platforms.

 "The Object Design relationship is an example of how Digital is
 partnering with leading software vendors to offer customers a choice of
 the best open client/server solutions," said William R. Demmer, vice
 president of the Software Business Group at Digital. "ObjectStore is an
 important addition to our total enterprise object offering.  The
 combination of ObjectStore's advanced features with Alpha AXP's
 industry-leading performance provides customers a potent platform for
 today's applications."

 For example, EDS, a joint customer of Object Design and Digital, is
 building PORTOS, a Portable Common Tool Environment (PCTE) repository
 for the software development market, using ObjectStore on Alpha AXP
 systems. PORTOS provides an open standards framework for integrating
 distributed CASE tools into a unified software engineering environment,
 using ObjectStore to provide the underlying distributed storage
 mechanism.

 "ObjectStore's availability on Alpha AXP is great news for us and our
 customers because we can combine the high performance of ObjectStore
 with the power and flexibility that comes with a 64-bit environment,"
 said Jonathan Tinkler, Software Engineering Manager at EDS UK.
 "Digital's leading position in the software development market makes
 Alpha AXP a very important platform for our product. "

 "With many of our key customers moving to Alpha AXP, porting
 ObjectStore to Digital's leading platforms was a strategic and
 logical move for us," said William Blundon, vice president of marketing
 at Object Design. "ObjectStore is used in very technically demanding
 applications and the Alpha AXP platform will provide the address space,
 performance and scalability customers want for modern object oriented
 applications."

 ObjectStore features distribution and transaction management for
 concurrent access to objects among members of a workgroup. It also
 offers state-of-the-art database functions such as data integrity,
 version control, query processing and a complete multi-client/
 multi-server architecture.

 Production versions of ObjectStore will ship in December for DEC OSF/1
 for Alpha AXP systems, in September for OpenVMS for Alpha AXP systems,
